The fluid solver — the GLSL shaders and the GPU simulation pipeline
(advection, divergence, curl, vorticity, Jacobi pressure solve, gradient
subtract) — is adapted from Pavel Dobryakov's MIT-licensed work. The
underlying technique originates with NVIDIA GPU Gems, Chapter 38,
"Fast Fluid Dynamics Simulation on the GPU."

Original work in this repository (MIT, Taha Bakri):
the preset system, the live controls panel, the reduced-motion and
pause-on-blur handling, the fluid-cursor wrapper module, and the
editorial type-inversion demo page.
